.\" Manpage for runabs.sh
.\" To install:  cp runabs.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/  &&  mandb
.\" To preview:  man -l runabs.1
.TH RUNABS 1 "May 2026" "runabs.sh 4.0.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runabs.sh \- run Audiobookshelf server with Node.js or Bun
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runabs.sh
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ FLAGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B runabs.sh
is a strict POSIX shell script that clones, builds, and runs
.UR https://www.audiobookshelf.org
Audiobookshelf
.UE ,
a self-hosted audiobook and podcast server.
.PP
The script supports both Node.js (the upstream-supported runtime) and Bun
(faster, but requires a Socket.IO patch).  It handles cross-platform autostart
(launchd on macOS, systemd user units on Linux, crontab \fB@reboot\fR
elsewhere), unicode-aware search (via the nunicode SQLite extension),
log rotation, and configuration via environment variables or
.B .env
files.
.PP
The script runs under
.BR sh ,
.BR dash ,
.BR ash ,
.BR bash ,
.BR ksh ,
.BR posh ,
and
.BR busybox\ ash .
No bashisms.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start Audiobookshelf as a daemon (default if no command is given).
The PID is written to
.IR $ABS_ROOT/audiobookshelf.pid .
Output goes to
.IR $ABS_ROOT/audiobookshelf.log .
.TP
.B foreground
Run Audiobookshelf in the current terminal with file-watch (auto-reload on
source changes).  Useful for first-time setup or debugging.
Aliases:
.BR run ,
.BR fg .
.TP
.B stop
Stop the running daemon.  Sends SIGTERM, waits up to 5 seconds, then
escalates to SIGKILL.
.TP
.B restart
Stop the running daemon (if any) then start a new one.  Pulls upstream
changes first if
.B ABS_AUTO_UPDATE=true
(default) or
.B \-\-update
is passed.
.TP
.B status
Report whether the daemon is running and, if so, its PID.
.TP
.B logs
Tail the daemon log (\fItail -f\fR).
.TP
.B check\-update
Compare the local repository\(aqs HEAD with
.B origin
and print a notice if an upstream update is available.  Does not pull.
.TP
.B check\-config
Validate the current configuration and print a detailed report covering
paths, network, binaries, runtime, features, ABS config, updates, logs,
and autostart.  Exits non-zero if any validation fails.
Alias:
.BR config .
.TP
.B install\-service
Install an autostart service appropriate to the platform: launchd on macOS,
a systemd user unit on Linux (when available), otherwise a
.B @reboot
crontab entry.  The runtime path and
.B ABS_AUTO_UPDATE
flag are baked into the service so behaviour stays stable.
Alias:
.BR install .
.TP
.B uninstall\-service
Remove the autostart service if installed.  Alias:
.BR uninstall .
.TP
.B init\-config
Write a commented
.B .env
template to
.IR $ABS_ROOT/.env .
With
.BR \-\-home ,
writes
.I ~/.env_abs
instead.
Alias:
.BR init .
.TP
.BR rebuild\-sqlite ", " rebuild\-sqlite3
Force a rebuild of the
.B sqlite3
native binding inside the ABS repository.  Useful only under the Bun
runtime: Bun's
.B bun install
sometimes skips the postinstall step that compiles
.IR node_sqlite3.node ,
which prevents Audiobookshelf from loading the unicode search extension
.RI ( libnusqlite3 ).
Internally runs
.B npm rebuild sqlite3
against the existing installation.  No-op under Node.js (where the
binding is already built by
.BR "npm install" ).
The rebuild requires
.B npm
to be installed; the rebuild process itself does not run Node.
.TP
.B version
Print the script version and exit.
.TP
.B help
Print the help screen and exit.
.SH FLAGS
.SS Mode
.TP
.BR \-\-dev ", " \-d
Run Audiobookshelf in development mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-prod ", " \-p
Run in production mode (default).
.SS Updates
.TP
.B \-\-update
Pull upstream changes before starting.  Used when
.B ABS_AUTO_UPDATE=false
to opt in for a single run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update
Skip pulling upstream changes.  Used when
.B ABS_AUTO_UPDATE=true
(default) to opt out for a single run.
.SS init-config
.TP
.B \-\-home
With
.BR init\-config ,
writes the template to
.I ~/.env_abs
instead of
.IR $ABS_ROOT/.env .
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the help screen.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the script version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read in this order, highest priority first:
.IP 1. 4
Environment variables set in the shell or service definition.
.IP 2. 4
.IR ~/.env_abs " (user-global)."
.IP 3. 4
.I .env
next to the script (directory-local).
.IP 4. 4
Hardcoded defaults in the script.
.PP
Both env files are
.I sourced
by the shell, so they use POSIX shell syntax:
.B VAR="value"
per line, comments with
.BR # .
.SS Environment variables
.TP
.B ABS_ROOT
Root directory for all Audiobookshelf data (repo clone, config, metadata,
logs).  Default:
.IR $HOME/audiobookshelf .
.TP
.B ABS_HOST
IP address or hostname to bind the server to.  Empty (default) binds to all
interfaces (0.0.0.0).
.TP
.B ABS_HOSTNAME
Hostname used in the displayed access URL.  Empty (default) uses the system
hostname.
.TP
.B ABS_PORT
TCP port to listen on.  Default: 13378.  Must be in 1..65535.
.TP
.B ABS_CONFIG_PATH
Configuration directory, relative to
.BR ABS_ROOT .
Default:
.BR config .
.TP
.B ABS_METADATA_PATH
Metadata directory, relative to
.BR ABS_ROOT .
Default:
.BR metadata .
.TP
.BR ABS_FFMPEG ", " ABS_FFPROBE
Absolute paths to
.B ffmpeg
and
.BR ffprobe .
Empty (default) auto-detects from
.BR PATH .
On Apple Silicon, the script auto-detects to avoid Audiobookshelf\(aqs
x86_64 download.
.TP
.B ABS_SKIP_BINARIES_CHECK
When set, skip Audiobookshelf\(aqs internal ffmpeg/ffprobe check.  Useful
when binaries are at non-standard paths.
.TP
.B ABS_NUNICODE_PATH
Absolute path to the nusqlite3 unicode search extension.  Empty (default)
triggers an automatic download matching the host platform and
architecture.
.TP
.B ABS_ALLOW_IFRAME
When
.BR true / 1 ,
allow Audiobookshelf to be embedded in an iframe (security risk).
.TP
.B ABS_BACKUP_PATH
Backup directory override.  Empty (default) uses Audiobookshelf\(aqs internal
default.
.TP
.B ABS_ROUTER_BASE_PATH
URL subpath for the web UI.  Default:
.BR /audiobookshelf .
Set to the empty string to serve at root.
.TP
.B ABS_REACT_CLIENT_PATH
Path to an experimental React client build (development feature).
.TP
.B ABS_ALLOW_CORS
When
.BR 1 / true ,
allow cross-origin requests.
.TP
.B ABS_SSRF_WHITELIST
Comma-separated list of hosts/CIDRs allowed past the SSRF filter.
.TP
.B ABS_DISABLE_SSRF
When
.BR 1 / true ,
disable the SSRF filter entirely (security risk).
.TP
.B ABS_JWT_SECRET
JWT signing key.  Empty (default) lets Audiobookshelf auto-generate one.
At least 32 characters recommended.
.TP
.B ABS_RUNTIME
Runtime selection:
.BR node ,
.BR bun ,
or an absolute path to a binary.  Empty (default) prompts on first run and
persists the choice to
.IR $ABS_ROOT/.runtime .
.IP
If
.B bun
is selected and not installed, the script offers to run Bun\(aqs official
installer after explicit user consent.
If
.B node
is selected and not installed, the script prints platform-appropriate
install instructions and exits; Node.js is never auto-installed.
.TP
.B ABS_AUTO_UPDATE
When
.B true
(default), every
.BR start / restart / foreground
pulls upstream changes first.  Override per-run with
.B \-\-update
or
.BR \-\-no\-update .
.TP
.B ABS_LOG_ROTATE
Log rotation threshold.  Accepts:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A bare number, interpreted as megabytes (e.g.
.BR 50 ).
.IP \(bu 2
A size with unit:
.BR K / KB / KiB ,
.BR M / MB / MiB ,
.BR G / GB / GiB
(e.g.
.BR 100M ,
.BR 1G ).
Units are case-insensitive and binary (powers of 1024).
.IP \(bu 2
An age in days (e.g.
.BR 30d ).
Rotates when the active log file is older than N days.
.RE
.IP
Only the active log is rotated, to
.IR audiobookshelf.log.1 .
Any existing
.B .1
file is overwritten (single-generation rotation).
Default:
.BR 50M .
.TP
.B ABS_BUN_SQLITE_REBUILD
Controls when the script rebuilds the
.B sqlite3
native binding under the Bun runtime (see the
.B rebuild\-sqlite
command).  Values:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B auto
(default): rebuild only if
.I node_sqlite3.node
is missing after
.BR "bun install" .
.IP \(bu 2
.BR always :
rebuild on every install regardless.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR never :
do nothing; warn if the binding is missing.
.RE
.IP
Ignored under Node.js (where
.B npm install
builds the binding natively).
.TP
.B ABS_DEBUG
If set to a non-empty, non-zero value, enables shell xtrace
.RB ( "set -o xtrace" )
for the duration of the run.  Equivalent to passing
.B \-\-debug
on the command line.  Useful for troubleshooting unexpected behavior;
output goes to stderr and is verbose.  Default: unset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $ABS_ROOT/audiobookshelf/
Cloned Audiobookshelf source tree.
.TP
.I $ABS_ROOT/audiobookshelf.pid
Daemon PID file.
.TP
.I $ABS_ROOT/audiobookshelf.log
Daemon log (created on first daemon start).
.TP
.I $ABS_ROOT/audiobookshelf.log.1
Previous log after rotation.
.TP
.I $ABS_ROOT/.runtime
Persisted runtime choice (absolute path to
.B node
or
.BR bun ).
.TP
.I $ABS_ROOT/.runabs.lock
Per-installation lock directory.  Removed automatically on exit.
.TP
.I $ABS_ROOT/.env
Directory-local configuration (overridden by environment).
.TP
.I ~/.env_abs
User-global configuration.
.TP
.I ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.audiobookshelf.server.plist
launchd service definition (macOS).
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/audiobookshelf.service
systemd user unit (Linux).
.TP
.I ~/.audiobookshelf-autostart.sh
Generic crontab wrapper script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic error: invalid argument, validation failure, missing dependency,
daemon failed to start, or service already installed.
.TP
.B 129
Hung up (SIGHUP).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (SIGINT, e.g. Ctrl+C).
.TP
.B 143
Terminated (SIGTERM).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run in foreground for the first time, to see each setup step:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
runabs.sh foreground
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start as a daemon on a non-default port:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
ABS_PORT=8080 runabs.sh start
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write a configuration template and edit it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
runabs.sh init\-config
$EDITOR \fI$HOME/audiobookshelf/.env\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install the platform autostart service:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
runabs.sh install\-service
.fi
.RE
.PP
Restart after pulling upstream changes:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
runabs.sh restart \-\-update
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rotate logs by age instead of size, with output in JSON-friendly form:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
ABS_LOG_ROTATE=30d runabs.sh check\-config
.fi
.RE
.PP
Override a runtime, persisting the choice:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
ABS_RUNTIME=bun runabs.sh start
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTOSTART SERVICE
The
.B install\-service
command installs a service appropriate to the operating system:
.IP \(bu 4
macOS: a launchd
.B LaunchAgent
at
.IR ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.audiobookshelf.server.plist .
.IP \(bu 4
Linux (with systemd available): a systemd user unit at
.IR ~/.config/systemd/user/audiobookshelf.service .
Manage with
.BR "systemctl --user {start|stop|status} audiobookshelf" .
.IP \(bu 4
Other platforms (or Linux without systemd): a POSIX wrapper at
.I ~/.audiobookshelf\-autostart.sh
registered as a
.B @reboot
entry in the user\(aqs crontab.
.PP
The chosen runtime path and the
.B ABS_AUTO_UPDATE
value at install time are baked into the service definition.  Changes to
.B .env
files are picked up at the next service start; changes to the runtime
require
.B uninstall\-service
followed by
.BR install\-service .
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The
.B check\-config
command is the primary diagnostic tool.  It validates every configuration
variable and reports per-section status with clear symbols
(\fB[OK]\fR, \fB[!]\fR, \fB[ERR]\fR, \fB[->]\fR), exiting non-zero on
failure.
.PP
On daemon startup, the script polls for 5 seconds.  If the process dies
within that window, the last 20 log lines are dumped to stderr and the
script exits 1.  This catches port conflicts, missing dependencies, and
configuration errors that survive validation.
.SH SECURITY
The script generates a Node.js configuration file
.RB ( dev.js )
that embeds configuration values as single-quoted JS literals.  All string
values are validated to reject single quotes, double quotes, backslashes,
and newlines before generation.  Path values are validated to be absolute.
Boolean values are validated against a fixed set.  Hostnames are validated
against RFC 1123 syntax; IP addresses against strict IPv4/IPv6 patterns
(IPv4 rejects leading zeros to prevent octal interpretation).
.PP
Runtime installation is asymmetric.
.B Bun
can be installed by the script via Bun\(aqs official
.B curl|bash
installer, but only after explicit consent at an interactive prompt;
non-TTY runs with Bun missing fail with manual installation instructions.
.B Node.js
is
.I never
auto-installed; if selected and missing, the script prints
platform-appropriate install instructions and exits.
.PP
The script never modifies system files outside of
.B ABS_ROOT
and the user-scoped service directories listed under
.BR FILES .
.SH PORTABILITY
The script targets strict POSIX shell.  Features used only when available:
.IP \(bu 4
.B set \-o pipefail
is enabled when supported and silently skipped on shells without it
(e.g. strict POSIX
.BR posh ).
.IP \(bu 4
.B readlink
is used for symlink resolution if present; otherwise the script falls back
to direct path resolution.
.IP \(bu 4
Network IP detection uses
.BR route / ipconfig
on macOS,
.BR ip / ifconfig / "hostname \-I"
on Linux, with graceful degradation if none is available.
.IP \(bu 4
Port-in-use detection uses
.BR lsof ,
.BR ss ,
or
.BR netstat
in that order.
